little bit of time — lessons from spending&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:48:40.800 --> 03:48:46.480
more than a million dollars on coaching.
I've got all sorts of bullets here: CEO coach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:48:46.479 --> 03:48:50.319
biz coach, boxing coach, therapist, health&nbsp;
coach, marketing coach, dating coach (three&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:48:50.319 --> 03:48:57.359
different ones), Hebrew and now Spanish coach.&nbsp;
The question I want to ask is related to all&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:48:57.359 --> 03:49:02.599
these inputs, because we also talked about&nbsp;
the top three, bottom three, the weekly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:49:02.600 --> 03:49:08.760
the monthly, the Q1, the this, the that.
What we were talking about as we took a&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:49:08.760 --> 03:49:13.960
break a little bit ago just for a bathroom&nbsp;
break, I've seen many examples of people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:49:13.960 --> 03:49:17.960
including myself, get inundated with inputs.&nbsp;
This happens also when people read too many&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:49:17.960 --> 03:49:22.239
books or they have too many advisors for this&nbsp;
startup. Now, they have 20 people they respect&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:49:22.239 --> 03:49:29.239
or 10 people they respect, even four people they&nbsp;
respect, giving them conflicting recommendations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:49:29.239 --> 03:49:34.000
or it's just too many recommendations. It's&nbsp;
like if you have 100 new years' resolutions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:49:34.000 --> 03:49:39.560
you have no new year's resolutions. So the first&nbsp;
thing I'm curious about is how, for yourself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:49:39.560 --> 03:49:47.428
do you choose what to act on outside of the&nbsp;
business KPIs and stuff, let's just say?&nbsp;

03:49:47.427 --> 03:49:54.000
Noah Kagan: Let's break these down. Let's take my&nbsp;
marketing coach. So I work with Moody Glasgow and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:49:54.000 --> 03:49:59.040
cold messaged him on LinkedIn. Now when you think&nbsp;
about coaching, I think instead of having mentors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:49:59.040 --> 03:50:03.800
let's have very specific coaches in very specific&nbsp;
areas that I'm weak in, or the people around me.&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:50:03.800 --> 03:50:07.320
We have a lot of coaches for the team. Almost&nbsp;
every single leader in the executive team of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:50:07.319 --> 03:50:12.880
AppSumo has a coach. With Moody, it was going&nbsp;
to him and saying, "I'm not as strong on some&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:50:12.880 --> 03:50:17.400
of the data stuff. I'm not as strong as some of&nbsp;
the marketing research stuff and branding stuff.&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:50:17.399 --> 03:50:21.799
Those are my specific areas of need and,&nbsp;
when we meet, let's really focus on that."&nbsp;

03:50:21.800 --> 03:50:26.199
Now, this is really the interesting caveat with&nbsp;
coaches. You're getting a coach because it's the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:50:26.199 --> 03:50:31.120
things you don't want to do or the things you're&nbsp;
not aware of, and so you have to be mindful of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:50:31.120 --> 03:50:37.439
resistance. The resistance is almost always the&nbsp;
direction I've noticed that ends up happening&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:50:37.439 --> 03:50:43.519
and I just maybe don't always do it right away.
So Moody, for instance, is, "Really want to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:50:43.520 --> 03:50:47.320
a lot of surveys." I'm like, "Moody, I don't&nbsp;
do surveys, man. Just let me go put up some&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:50:47.319 --> 03:50:52.040
ads. Let's do more affiliate marketing. Let's do&nbsp;
more video ambassador sponsorship." He's like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:50:52.040 --> 03:50:55.680
"Who are you doing that for?" "I don't know,&nbsp;
dude. I don't want to do research. Let's go do&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:50:55.680 --> 03:51:00.920
stuff. I'm a doer." And so his balance of&nbsp;
these things is saying, "Let's go do some&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:51:00.920 --> 03:51:05.279
research so we know who we're doing it for&nbsp;
and be very specific who the customer is."&nbsp;

03:51:05.279 --> 03:51:09.159
Now you asked the question of inputs. I think&nbsp;
the inputs need to tie to your main priorities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:51:09.159 --> 03:51:13.599
and that's it. So what is the priorities I'm&nbsp;
saying? So within our marketing team right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:51:13.600 --> 03:51:18.160
it's getting a VP of marketing, it's content,&nbsp;
and it's brand awareness. Also, video&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:51:18.159 --> 03:51:23.359
ambassadors — getting more of those. And so within&nbsp;
inputs, I'm just like, I'm specifically going over&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:51:23.359 --> 03:51:26.759
those specific problems and saying, "Walk me&nbsp;
through how you're normally thinking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:51:26.760 --> 03:51:30.400
solving this." And then, he normally is coaching&nbsp;
me and we're having a discussion around it.&nbsp;

03:51:30.399 --> 03:51:34.439
What I have found with most of the inputs is&nbsp;
that I end up doing them almost always six&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:51:34.439 --> 03:51:39.239
months later because I resist them and I'm going&nbsp;
to do what I want to do anyways. Just like most&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:51:39.239 --> 03:51:44.359
people here maybe want to start business their way&nbsp;
and six months later they think about the coach.&nbsp;

03:51:44.359 --> 03:51:48.159
The other thing with him specifically on&nbsp;
ticking inputs, I record all my coaching calls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:51:48.159 --> 03:51:52.159
every single one, every single one. And then I&nbsp;
go and listen to them again, not all the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:51:52.159 --> 03:51:57.319
but selectively depending on if I'm trying to&nbsp;
learn something, noticing how I'm resisting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:51:57.319 --> 03:52:01.960
noticing where I'm paying attention. That helps&nbsp;
me be able to be a better student with my coach.&nbsp;

03:52:02.800 --> 03:52:07.440
So, coming back full circle with coaching in&nbsp;
general, how to choose the input, I think it&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:52:07.439 --> 03:52:10.159
comes back to my priorities and the&nbsp;
specific problems I'm coming to them&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:52:10.159 --> 03:52:14.027
with. And a lot of times it's then sitting&nbsp;
with the answer that they bring back to me.&nbsp;

03:52:14.027 --> 03:52:18.748
Tim Ferriss: As one example from the bullet list,&nbsp;
so CEO coach, would that be Dan from Reboot?&nbsp;

03:52:18.748 --> 03:52:23.239
Noah Kagan: That's Dan Putt as well&nbsp;
as Ayman Al-Abdullah. Dan is more&nbsp;&nbsp;

