03:53:05.199 --> 03:53:08.960
of popular products. So Mailchimp, we have an&nbsp;
alternative. Calendly, we have an alternative.&nbsp;

03:53:09.760 --> 03:53:15.400
I went to him and I said, 'Hey, let me walk over —&nbsp;
the one thing I'm uncertain of is 2024 and around&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:53:15.399 --> 03:53:21.679
what we should do with new products," and brought&nbsp;
it to him, walked over it. Now I'm so convinced&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:53:21.680 --> 03:53:24.680
that we need to build a bunch of new things. I'm&nbsp;
like, "Dude, this new stuff is going to be so&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:53:24.680 --> 03:53:28.440
sick. We're going to build a Loom alternative.&nbsp;
We're going to build this other product&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:53:28.439 --> 03:53:33.120
alternative, maybe a DocuSign alternative." And&nbsp;
because I have a mirror, I have him, and I like&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:53:33.120 --> 03:53:36.880
coaches who've done the things I want to do. He's&nbsp;
run the business. He's a former CEO. He's like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:53:36.880 --> 03:53:39.760
"No, what's working in your products that you&nbsp;
guys have built?" I'm like, "We have this one&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:53:39.760 --> 03:53:45.760
product. It's crushing it." "Okay, so you have a&nbsp;
product crushing it and you want to do a new one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

